The bug was caused by the power management functions `bcm_qspi_suspend` and `bcm_qspi_resume` being defined within an `#ifdef CONFIG_PM_SLEEP` directive, but referenced unconditionally in the code. This led to compilation errors when `CONFIG_PM_SLEEP` was not set, as the functions were undeclared in that context.

